  "id": "Compound::DB00425 - Gene::2566",
  "verbalization": "Zolpidem and Gabrg2 are linked through a complex network of molecular interactions and pharmacological pathways. The evidence suggests that Zolpidem binds to Gabra2, which is involved in benzodiazepine receptor activity, and Gabra2 is a component of the Gaba A receptor complex. This implies that Zolpidem may exert its effects through the Gaba A receptor, potentially modulating central nervous system activity. Additionally, Zolpidem is included in the category of Gaba A agonists, which includes Zaleplon, another compound that binds to Gabrg2. This indicates a broader pharmacological relationship between Zolpidem and Gabrg2, possibly through shared mechanisms in the Gaba A receptor pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Gabrg2 in mediating the sedative and hypnotic effects of Zolpidem and related compounds.",
